@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
<div class="policy-page">
<p><em>Last updated: September 30, 2026</em></p>

<p>
    This Privacy Policy explains what information WeGotThis ("we", "us", "the site") collects,
    how we use it, and the choices you have. By using the site, you agree to this policy.
</p>

<h2>1. Information we collect</h2>

<h3>Information you give us</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your username and password. Passwords are stored in hashed form, not as plain text.</li>
    <li><strong>Content you submit:</strong> goals you post, and your actions on other users' goals (completed or rejected). Goals are shown to other users along with your username.</li>
    <li><strong>Activity data:</strong> your token balance and related usage of the site.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>IP address:</strong> the internet address your device uses to connect to the site.</li>
    <li><strong>Date and time:</strong> timestamps of your visits, requests, and actions on the site.</li>
    <li><strong>Cookies:</strong> small files stored in your browser (see section 4).</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
<ul>
    <li>To create and manage your account and keep you logged in.</li>
    <li>To operate the site's features, such as showing goals, tracking tokens, and recording your actions.</li>
    <li>To keep the site secure, prevent abuse and fraud, and troubleshoot problems (for example, using IP addresses and timestamps).</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

<h2>3. Legal basis (for users in the EU/EEA and UK)</h2>
<p>
    We process your data to provide the service you requested (contract), for our legitimate interests in
    securing and improving the site, and where required, with your consent (for non-essential cookies, if any are used).
</p>

<h2>4. Cookies</h2>
<p>We use only the cookies needed for the site to work:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Authentication cookie:</strong> keeps you logged in between pages.</li>
    <li><strong>Antiforgery cookie:</strong> protects forms on the site from cross-site request forgery attacks.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    These are strictly necessary, so the site can't function properly without them. We do not currently use
    advertising or third-party analytics cookies. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings,
    but doing so will prevent you from logging in.
</p>

<h2>5. How long we keep your information</h2>
<p>
    We keep account information and content for as long as your account exists. IP addresses and access
    timestamps are kept only as long as needed for security and troubleshooting, then deleted
    (<strong>after 90 days</strong>). You can ask us to delete your account and data at any time.
</p>

<h2>6. Sharing your information</h2>
<p>
    We do not sell or rent your personal information. We may share it only with hosting and infrastructure
    providers that run the site on our behalf, or when required by law or to protect the rights and safety of
    users and the site. Your username and the goals you submit are visible to other logged-in users.
</p>

<h2>7. Security</h2>
<p>
    We take reasonable steps to protect your information, including password hashing and secure connections.
    No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
</p>

<h2>8. Your rights</h2>
<p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you,</li>
    <li>correct inaccurate data,</li>
    <li>delete your data,</li>
    <li>object to or restrict certain processing, and</li>
    <li>receive a copy of your data in a portable format.</li>
</ul>
<p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us using the details below.</p>

<h2>9. Children</h2>
<p>
    The site is not intended for children under 13 (or 16 where required by local law).
    We do not knowingly collect information from children. If you believe a child has given us
    personal data, contact us and we will delete it.
</p>

<h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top shows when it
    last changed. Continued use of the site after changes means you accept the updated policy.
</p>

<h2>11. Contact us</h2>
<p>
    Questions or requests about this policy or your data: <strong>eliworkedonthat@gmail.com</strong>
</p>
</div>